            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0552" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">871.001/4–2545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-25T20:00:00+02:00">April 25, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 25—4:23 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4218. I conveyed to the Prime Minister the information in your 2930 of April 14
                    concerning the protection of the Rumanian Royal Family. Mr. Churchill has now
                    informed me that he feels shelter should not be denied the King and Queen if
                    they should seek it, and that the British representatives in Bucharest have been
                    instructed to give them sanctuary if it is requested. He feels deeply on this
                    subject.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
